  "novel": "Barney [[slept|sleep]] with Robin, [[devastating|devastate]] Ted. Their [[friendship|friendship]] [[fractured|fracture]] in an [[instant|instant]].\n\n\"You [[betrayed|betray]] me,\" Ted [[whispered|whisper]], his voice [[shaking|shake]] with [[anger|anger]]. \"You knew how I felt.\"\n\nBarney [[pleaded|plead]] for [[forgiveness|forgiveness]]. \"It just happened,\" he said. But Ted [[refused|refuse]] to listen.\n\nLily [[tried|try]] to [[mediate|mediate]]. \"People make [[mistakes|mistake]],\" she said. But the [[damage|damage]] was done.\n\nMeanwhile, a [[goat|goat]] [[wandered|wander]] into the apartment and ate Marshall's [[towel|towel]]. The [[absurd|absurd]] scene symbolized the chaos in their lives.\n\nWeeks passed. The guilt gnawed at Barney. He realized that betrayal had a price — not just Ted's friendship, but his own soul. Some wounds, like the goat's visit, were unexpected and impossible to explain.",
